From 468a4814a4ed34384ad8c685a0651920add1b206 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tpchgen): O(1) row skips, cheaper modulus, no per-row
 color copy

Three drop-in changes to the core random number generation; generated
values are unchanged.

- RowRandomInt::advance_seed memoizes MULTIPLIER^count. row_finished
  almost always skips the same number of unused seeds, so finishing a
  row becomes one multiply instead of a square-and-multiply loop, for
  every column stream on every row.
- next_rand reduces mod 2^31-1 by folding (2^31 = 1 mod M) instead of
  the multiply-high sequence the compiler emits for `%`.
- RandomStringSequence (p_name) no longer copies all 92 colors into a
  Vec per row: a partial Fisher-Yates that tracks only the swapped
  positions gives the same draws and result.

Unit tests compare each against the original algorithm; the existing
reference-data integration tests pass unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UeniBBPwY58QJUuZK9Pcd5
